    {
      "id": "east-front",
      "cardSha256": "ed9c2df4350546dd3fc20214b3b7eaf036d4503c01a27751bfeb1cc3d5bdb19e",
      "side": "russian",
      "name": "East front",
      "idea": "The weight faces the assault engineers and Kampfgruppe Tienham: two squads in each hex of the east face with the HMG under the 9-2 at Y5 and both MMG, and two more at X5. The west is two squads with an LMG at W4 and two at X3. W5, X2, and the centre hold only Dummies, the centre four of them, so it looks like the reserve.",
      "givesUp": "W5, X2, and X4 are not defended: a German squad that enters them takes their Control, and there is no reserve behind the two faces.",
      "terrain": [
        "The east face looks at the assault engineers' buildings: Y3, Y4, and Y5 see AA4 at range 2, Y4 and Y5 see AA5 at range 2, and Y5 and X5 see Y7 and Z6 at range 2.",
        "The west face looks at Kampfgruppe Stahler's building U3: W4, X2, and X3 see V2 at range 2, W4 sees U3 at range 2, and X2, X3, and W5 see U3 at range 3.",
        "X4, the centre hex, has no LOS to or from any German setup Location, nor to any hex next to the building.",
        "Of the hexes held only by Dummies, W5 is seen from U3 at range 3 and from S5 and U8 at 4, X2 from V2 at range 2, U3 at 3, and T4 at 4, and X4 from nowhere.",
        "The three plans of this card show the same number of counters in every hex of the Works (W4 3, W5 3, X2 2, X3 2, X4 4, X5 2, Y3 3, Y4 3, Y5 3), and every counter is a \"?\", so the Germans cannot tell from the stacks which plan was used. Each holds six hexes with real units and three with Dummies only; the plans differ in which three. X3 and X5 hold real units in all three, so those two hexes are no secret.",
        "The card makes X3 a Factory (SSR 5), which has no upper levels, so every counter stands at ground level, although the board's data gives the building levels 1 and 2.",
        "The side that Controls six of the building's nine hexes (W4, W5, X2, X3, X4, X5, Y3, Y4, Y5) at game end wins; the Russians Control all nine at the start."
      ],
