      "id": "three-sides",
      "cardSha256": "ed9c2df4350546dd3fc20214b3b7eaf036d4503c01a27751bfeb1cc3d5bdb19e",
      "side": "german",
      "name": "Three sides",
      "idea": "Every hex of the Works shows the same \"?\" whichever plan the Russians used, so the Germans press three faces at once and learn by fire which stacks are real. All six engineer squads start unseen at BB4, on two levels: the 10-3 with both flamethrowers and three demolition charges at ground level, the two LMG and the fourth charge upstairs. Kampfgruppe Tienham fires from the upper floor of Z6 and Y7 on X5 and Y5 at range 2, with the HMG under the 10-2, and keeps two squads and the 8-0 back at Y8. Kampfgruppe Stahler stands under \"?\" at V2 and U3, two hexes from the west face, with two squads behind at U2, and its nine Dummies fill T4, S5, and T7 so that it looks twice its size.",
      "givesUp": "The force is spread over three faces, so no face has the weight to break in alone; the engineers start three hexes from the Works; and the Dummies fool nobody once they are fired on. If the die roll gives the Russians the first move, the stacks at Z6 and Y7 take their Prep Fire with no \"?\".",
      "terrain": [
        "BB4 is seen from no hex of the Works, at any level, and has a stairwell; it is three hexes from Y4.",
        "Z6 and Y7 see X5 and Y5 at range 2; Y8, behind them, is seen from no hex of the Works.",
        "V2 sees W4, X2, and X3 at range 2; U3 sees W4 at range 2 and W5, X2, and X3 at range 3; U2 is seen from no hex of the Works.",
        "Of the Dummy hexes, T4 is seen from X2 at range 4, S5 from W5 at range 4, and T7 from X5 at range 4: each is in a Russian LOS, so the Russians see a \"?\" stack there.",
        "The plan uses all 12 of Kampfgruppe Stahler's \"?\": 3 for its concealed stacks and 9 Dummies.",
        "The stacks at BB4 and Y8 are out of every Russian LOS, so each may take a \"?\" once every group has set up (A12.12), whichever plan the Russians used.",
        "The two German plans of this card look the same to the Russians: the same stacks in the same Locations, with the same counters on top and the same \"?\". They differ in which of Kampfgruppe Stahler's \"?\" stacks are real, where the flamethrowers and the machine guns are, and which leader stands where.",
        "The side that Controls six of the building's nine hexes (W4, W5, X2, X3, X4, X5, Y3, Y4, Y5) at game end wins; the Russians Control all nine at the start."
      ],
