    {
      "id": "feint-west",
      "cardSha256": "ed9c2df4350546dd3fc20214b3b7eaf036d4503c01a27751bfeb1cc3d5bdb19e",
      "side": "german",
      "name": "Feint west",
      "idea": "The stacks that seem ready to rush the west face, at V2, U3, and U2, are Kampfgruppe Stahler's nine Dummies. Its real force stands back at T4, S5, and T7 as a fire base: both MMG under the 9-2 at T4, three squads with the LMG at S5, two squads and the 8-1 at T7, each four hexes from the Works. The weight is in the south-east: Kampfgruppe Tienham's HMG fires from Y7 under the 10-2, and the engineers start unseen at BB4 with a flamethrower on each level, so one may go by the east face and one round to the south.",
      "givesUp": "Nothing real stands within three hexes of the west face, so the west is fire only until Stahler closes; a Russian player who ignores the Dummies loses nothing in the west. If the die roll gives the Russians the first move, the stacks at Z6 and Y7 take their Prep Fire with no \"?\".",
      "terrain": [
        "T4 sees X2 at range 4, S5 sees W5 at range 4, and T7 sees X5 at range 4, each from level 1; a 4-6-7 fires at full strength to range 6 and an MMG to 12.",
        "Of the Dummy hexes, V2 is seen from W4, X2, and X3 at range 2 and U3 from W4 at range 2 and W5, X2, and X3 at range 3, so the Russians see \"?\" stacks two hexes from the west face; U2 is seen from no hex of the Works.",
        "Z6 and Y7 see X5 and Y5 at range 2; Y8, behind them, is seen from no hex of the Works.",
        "BB4 is seen from no hex of the Works, at any level, and has a stairwell; it is three hexes from Y4.",
        "The plan uses all 12 of Kampfgruppe Stahler's \"?\": 3 for its concealed stacks and 9 Dummies.",
        "The stacks at BB4 and Y8 are out of every Russian LOS, so each may take a \"?\" once every group has set up (A12.12), whichever plan the Russians used.",
        "The two German plans of this card look the same to the Russians: the same stacks in the same Locations, with the same counters on top and the same \"?\". They differ in which of Kampfgruppe Stahler's \"?\" stacks are real, where the flamethrowers and the machine guns are, and which leader stands where.",
        "The side that Controls six of the building's nine hexes (W4, W5, X2, X3, X4, X5, Y3, Y4, Y5) at game end wins; the Russians Control all nine at the start."
      ],
